als on the lateral cephalothorax surface that rub against tubecles on the inner surface of the femur of leg 1.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Stridulatory%20structures/Stridulator_Afraflacilla.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Stridulatory%20structures/Stridulator_Afraflacilla.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":49,"uid":"d96dd789-8180-4cf9-b22c-4ff222539166","name":"absent","type":0,"feature":33,"images":[{"caption":"Example where there is no local prominence of the cephalothorax<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Median%20prominance/Median_prominence_absent%20.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Median%20prominance/Median_prominence_absent%20.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":50,"uid":"b1960f47-5a99-47f4-a62f-59c5523bb7b5","name":"present","type":0,"feature":33,"images":[{"caption":"Example where there is a local prominence of the cephalothorax<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Median%20prominance/Median_prominence_present.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Median%20prominance/Median_prominence_present.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":51,"uid":"bf0271b3-dd33-4e61-a6ad-6e75e2178451","name":"very high carapace","type":0,"feature":34,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of species with a very high cephalothorax<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSI","comments":"The cephalothorax is much higher than the abdomen.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_very_high.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_very_high.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":52,"uid":"f55fbe15-1343-4867-b1bc-2401af9482d9","name":"high carapace","type":0,"feature":34,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of species with a high cephalothorax<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB)","comments":"Curves to a central peak, never much higher than abdomen.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_%20high.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_%20high.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":53,"uid":"84c0c917-242e-4924-9b67-44261e1c1b88","name":"low carapace","type":0,"feature":34,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of species with a low cephalothorax<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB)","comments":"Cephalothorax almost completely flat to well behind the PLE","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_%20low.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_%20low.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":54,"uid":"df2712f8-3ddb-4ec0-bbf9-67309ad3166c","name":"very low carapace","type":0,"feature":34,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of species with a very low cephalothorax<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag.)","comments":"Cephalothora is very flat, and thin from the side.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_very_low.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Outline%20of%20cephalothorax%20from%20side/Carapace_height_very_low.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":55,"uid":"e79d33a0-20aa-4f68-9d3a-8ebfa5efff8a","name":"Upper surface flat","type":0,"feature":35,"images":[{"caption":"Carapace flat until well behind posterior lateral eyes<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"Anterior eyes should be vertical when deciding.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Silhouette%20of%20cephalothorax/Silhouette_flat%201.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Silhouette%20of%20cephalothorax/Silhouette_flat%201.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":56,"uid":"6c8cdc1c-9f95-49cb-9b3d-ceca49dd2292","name":"Upper surface with highest point near PLE","type":0,"feature":35,"images":[{"caption":"Example of species where the carapace is highest near the PL Eyes<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB)","comments":"Anterior eyes should be vertical when deciding.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Silhouette%20of%20cephalothorax/Silhouette_peaks_near_PLE.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Silhouette%20of%20cephalothorax/Silhouette_peaks_near_PLE.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":57,"uid":"79c872cf-d746-4bf2-90ba-72145c37c450","name":"Upper surface tapers to rear along length","type":0,"feature":35,"images":[{"caption":"Slope starts at the anterior eyes and continues steadily backwards<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Anterior eyes should be vertical when deciding.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Silhouette%20of%20cephalothorax/Silhouette_slopes.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Silhouette%20of%20cephalothorax/Silhouette_slopes.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":58,"uid":"ac2bc06c-ec7c-47db-aec3-9c3532e05305","name":"thoracic slope gentle","type":0,"feature":36,"images":[{"caption":"Examples cephalorthax with a gentle rear slope<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"Anterior eyes should be vertical when deciding. Usually a gradual change in slope to less than 45 degrees.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20thoracic%20slope%20of%20cephalothorax/Thoracic_slope_gentle.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20thoracic%20slope%20of%20cephalothorax/Thoracic_slope_gentle.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":59,"uid":"b372dbae-2b8b-44e0-84d8-6e402f615f17","name":"thoracic slope steep","type":0,"feature":36,"images":[{"caption":"Example of cephalothorax with steep slope<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"Anterior eyes should be vertical when deciding. Usually a distinct change in slope to more than 45 degrees.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20thoracic%20slope%20of%20cephalothorax/Thoracic_slope_steep.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20thoracic%20slope%20of%20cephalothorax/Thoracic_slope_steep.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":60,"uid":"93dfb093-279f-4d6d-8802-6f8cf308c739","name":"thoracic slope abrupt","type":0,"feature":36,"images":[{"caption":"Example of cephalothorax with abrupt slope<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"Anterior eyes should be vertical when deciding. An abrupt change in slope to near vertical.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20thoracic%20slope%20of%20cephalothorax/Thoracic_slope_abrupt.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20thoracic%20slope%20of%20cephalothorax/Thoracic_slope_abrupt.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":61,"uid":"e22c0143-63a5-45be-9ace-71c9d210128c","name":"smooth","type":0,"feature":37,"images":[{"caption":"Example of smooth rear edge to Cephalothorax<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20edge%20of%20cephalothorax/Posterior_edge_smooth.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20edge%20of%20cephalothorax/Posterior_edge_smooth.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":62,"uid":"59c297d7-fd26-486f-91df-198372095da6","name":"crenellated","type":0,"feature":37,"images":[{"caption":"Example of crenellated rear edge to Cephalothorax<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20edge%20of%20cephalothorax/Posterior_edge_crenellated.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Posterior%20edge%20of%20cephalothorax/Posterior_edge_crenellated.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":63,"uid":"ad6837a0-f75e-4ef4-a78d-eb2a8bbcfd1c","name":"near vertical or rounded","type":0,"feature":38,"images":[{"caption":"Species with sides of cephalothorax near vertical (R) or rounded (L)<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Sides are straight or curve slightly outwards and then inwards approaching the lower edge. Ensure the face is vertical otherwise the bottom edge can appear rounded.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Sides%20of%20cephalothorax/sides_vertical_or_rounded.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Sides%20of%20cephalothorax/sides_vertical_or_rounded.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":64,"uid":"cf913b73-a0bd-46e5-aedb-f864b6e13c9f","name":"sloping outwards","type":0,"feature":38,"images":[{"caption":"Species showing the siders of the cephalothorax sloping outwards<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Much wider at the ventral edge; does not curve inwards towards the lower edge. Ensure the face is vertical otherwise the bottom edge can appear rounded.","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Sides%20of%20cephalothorax/sides_sloping.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Sides%20of%20cephalothorax/sides_sloping.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":65,"uid":"a77c4b06-9da3-414a-a297-2d695e302f09","name":"less than diameter of Anterior Lateral Eyes","type":0,"feature":39,"images":[{"caption":"Clupeal depth  narrow<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"The measurement is taken between the lower edge of the anterior median eyes (AME) and the nearest point on the lower edge of the of the clupeus and compared with the diameter of the anterior lateral eye (ALE).","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20depth/clupeus_depth%20small.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20depth/clupeus_depth%20small.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":66,"uid":"b27d6a05-b1bb-437e-bae0-34ed0ef7cd22","name":"about the diameter of Anterior Lateral Eyes","type":0,"feature":39,"images":[{"caption":"Clupeal depth  intermediate<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"The measurement is taken between the lower edge of the anterior median eyes (AME) and the nearest point on the lower edge of the of the clupeus and compared with the diameter of the anterior lateral eye (ALE).","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20depth/clupeus_depth.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20depth/clupeus_depth.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":67,"uid":"c898e9b2-24cd-4a0a-9d15-58386f959059","name":"more than diameter of Anterior Lateral Eyes","type":0,"feature":39,"images":[{"caption":"Clupeal depth broad<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"The measurement is taken between the lower edge of the anterior median eyes (AME) and the nearest point on the lower edge of the of the clupeus and compared with the diameter of the anterior lateral eye (ALE).","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20depth/clupeus_depth%20large.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20depth/clupeus_depth%20large.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":68,"uid":"be3d0aaa-3134-4192-8f87-862ec68b7d24","name":"no fringe","type":0,"feature":40,"images":[{"caption":"Example where there is no clupeal fringe<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20special%20features/clupeal_fringe_absent.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20special%20features/clupeal_fringe_absent.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":69,"uid":"b047d8fb-06fa-4ecb-bc6f-1eea0de55ecb","name":"sparse fringe on lower margin","type":0,"feature":40,"images":[{"caption":"Example where the clupeal fringe is sparse<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20special%20features/Clupeal_fringe_light.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20special%20features/Clupeal_fringe_light.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":70,"uid":"06784ec6-0080-42a4-bfef-43d099c371b7","name":"heavy fringe on lower margin","type":0,"feature":40,"images":[{"caption":"Example where the clupeal fringe is thick<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","path":"Images/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20special%20features/Clupeal_fringe_heavy.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Aspects%20of%20general%20morphology/Clupeus%20special%20features/Clupeal_fringe_heavy.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":71,"uid":"917a0d21-a864-489a-8bea-a82abcdaf791","name":"iridescent; in bands or lines","type":0,"feature":41,"images":[{"caption":"Specimens showing transverse or longitudinal bands<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) R. Whyte","comments":"Bands are clearly demarked strips of a different colour. They do not include diffuse fringing or whole large sections of colour difference, for example the rear half of the abdomen.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/Hairs_irridescent_in_lines.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/Hairs_irridescent_in_lines.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":72,"uid":"b613afba-27e2-4072-b5da-39831ff80b9b","name":"iridescent; not in bands or lines","type":0,"feature":41,"images":[{"caption":"Specimens showing iridescent hairs not in bands<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) R. Whyte & B. Baehr","comments":"Bands are clearly demarked strips of a different colour. They do not include diffuse fringing or whole large sections of colour difference, for example the rear half of the abdomen.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_irridescent_not_in_lines.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_irridescent_not_in_lines.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":73,"uid":"6e071320-2684-4392-bcf9-5a805e70a417","name":"non-iridescent; in bands or lines","type":0,"feature":41,"images":[{"caption":"Specimens showing non-iridescent hairs in bands or lines<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson(T) (CSIRO, MP), I. Macaulay","comments":"Bands are clearly demarked strips of a different colour. They do not include diffuse fringing or whole large sections of colour difference, for example the rear half of the abdomen .","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_not_irridescent_in_lines.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_not_irridescent_in_lines.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":74,"uid":"2bfe1907-f794-42f8-bcf8-c4db2d36bc3a","name":"non-iridescent; not in bands or lines","type":0,"feature":41,"images":[{"caption":"Specimens showing non-iridescent hairs not in lines or bands<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Bands are clearly demarked strips of a different colour. They do not include diffuse fringing or whole large sections of colour difference, for example the rear half of the abdomen or down the centre-line.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_not_irridescent_not_in_lines.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_not_irridescent_not_in_lines.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":75,"uid":"44cdeca3-a460-4032-9806-671560189f4c","name":"no hairs; shiny surface","type":0,"feature":41,"images":[{"caption":"Specimen showing abdomen without hairs<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) G.J. Anderson","comments":"The abdominal hairs can be rubbed off in preserved specimens.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_none.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Hairs%20in%20males/hairs_none.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":76,"uid":"6aa200e6-c497-48cf-be39-5458ac3c6fd8","name":"heart-shaped","type":0,"feature":42,"images":[{"caption":"Example of a species with a heart-shaped abdomen<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"Heart-shaped means an oval shape indented at the centre anteriorly and narrowing to a point posteriorly","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_heartshaped.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_heartshaped.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":77,"uid":"35d4727a-fda2-417d-a6f8-7c070927bce5","name":"ovate","type":0,"feature":42,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of species with ovate abdomens<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB), B.J. Richardson (R) (CSIRO, MP)","comments":"Abdomen can be swollen slightly towards the rear (posteriorly) or anteriorly or uniformly ovate. Abdomen less than 1.5x the length of the cephalothorax","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_ovate.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_ovate.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":78,"uid":"854f2426-cd99-4096-b7ba-a75c823b6b7d","name":"rounded to circular","type":0,"feature":42,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of species with rounded abdomens<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (L) (CSIRO), M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"Rounded includes approaching circular in shape (or widely ovate) and very nearly completely circular.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_round.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_round.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":79,"uid":"eaa25525-45df-4d9b-aaab-9aeeca542533","name":"with  flaps folded under (extended during courtship)","type":0,"feature":42,"images":[{"caption":"Example of a species with flaps on the abdomen (L) that fold away underneath (R)<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) J. Waldock (WAMP)","comments":"See Maratus for illustrations of the flaps extended.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_with_flaps.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_with_flaps.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":80,"uid":"5222f1e8-cf9b-471c-8253-ad40a50d11fe","name":"with constriction (ant-like)","type":0,"feature":42,"images":[{"caption":"Example of species with a constriction across the abdomen<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"The constriction is often not as marked as in this illustration","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_with_constriction.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_with_constriction.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":81,"uid":"ab2edfd9-29f2-4e3d-bffd-7361c09579ab","name":"elongated","type":0,"feature":42,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of species with elongated abdomens<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (AMS)","comments":"Elongate is essentially ovate but is always much lengthened, sometimes extremely so. Abdomen at least 1.5x the length of the cephalothorax.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_elongate.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_elongate.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":82,"uid":"ac85d92b-ab20-49b8-92e9-bdd68e0b1763","name":"narrowing evenly towards the rear","type":0,"feature":42,"images":[{"caption":"Example of species with a tapering abdomen<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO, MP)","comments":"Tapering is where the anterior part is wide, not substantially indented and then narrows gradually towards the rear, like an upside down pear.","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_tapers.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Abdomen%20shape/abdomen_tapers.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":83,"uid":"e44b2805-193c-4816-b906-df99c734c38d","name":"absent","type":0,"feature":43,"images":[{"caption":"Examples where there are no dorsal hair tufts on the abdomen<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB), B.J. Richardson (CSIRO) (MP)","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Dorsal%20tufts%20present/Dorsal_tufts_absent.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Dorsal%20tufts%20present/Dorsal_tufts_absent.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":84,"uid":"f4c988e4-50db-4eda-a1ba-d046c9b7f62e","name":"present","type":0,"feature":43,"images":[{"caption":"Examples where dorsal hair tufts present on the abdomen<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB), I. Macaulay","path":"Images/features/Abdomen/Dorsal%20tufts%20present/Hair_tufts_present.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Abdomen/Dorsal%20tufts%20present/Hair_tufts_present.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":85,"uid":"017aa37d-1faf-48a3-90f8-8985e146ef44","name":"much less than one third of abdomen length","type":0,"feature":44},{"id":86,"uid":"0cc324db-860d-43d4-9a30-a369f437f9bf","name":"one third of abdomen length","type":0,"feature":44},{"id":87,"uid":"ea29800a-435f-457a-88bf-c1f6b506866f","name":"without retrolateral protuberance","type":0,"feature":45,"images":[{"caption":"Example of endites without retrolateral protuberances<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","path":"Images/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Endite%20retrolateral%20protuberance/reterolateral_protuberence_absent.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Endite%20retrolateral%20protuberance/reterolateral_protuberence_absent.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":88,"uid":"d305960f-cc62-4c36-b9d6-f4ccf0d376c1","name":"with retrolateral protuberance","type":0,"feature":45,"images":[{"caption":"Example of retrolateral protuberance on the endite<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","path":"Images/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Endite%20retrolateral%20protuberance/retrolateral_protuberance_present.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Endite%20retrolateral%20protuberance/retrolateral_protuberance_present.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":89,"uid":"1e248c4d-9b4c-4203-a86a-8b837cc54fe1","name":"Slightly longer than wide","type":0,"feature":46,"images":[{"caption":"Example with a short labium<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","path":"Images/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Labium%20proportions/labium_short.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Labium%20proportions/labium_short.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":90,"uid":"63498296-3cac-4fff-8f15-45e3ed9a4be0","name":"Twice as long as wide","type":0,"feature":46,"images":[{"caption":"Example with a long endite<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","path":"Images/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Labium%20proportions/labium_extended.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Labium%20proportions/labium_extended.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":91,"uid":"4333f8e3-d0d0-4360-9322-58a53814063a","name":"Almost flat","type":0,"feature":47,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of a sternum with a distinct mound in the centre<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson CSIRO)","comments":"The sternum surface is flat or slightly convex.","path":"Images/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Sternum%20surface/sternum_without%20prominance.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Sternum%20surface/sternum_without%20prominance.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":92,"uid":"8493edc1-0eb6-4cdc-9284-c8cf9630d1d2","name":"with prominence","type":0,"feature":47,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of sternums with a distinct mound in the centre<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte, M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB)","comments":"Instead of being flat or slightly convex, the sternum has a low or high 'hill' in the centre.","path":"Images/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Sternum%20surface/sternum_with_prominance.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Ventral%20cephalothorax/Sternum%20surface/sternum_with_prominance.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":93,"uid":"a76bfaa6-0b8c-4bff-b670-95700c1a1c0a","name":"none","type":0,"feature":48,"images":[{"caption":"Example of chelae without  promarginal teeth<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Promarginal%20teeth/promarginal_teeth_none.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Promarginal%20teeth/promarginal_teeth_none.jpg","type":1}]},