 still less than 1.3x the face height.","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Shape%20in%20female/chelicera_female_long.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Shape%20in%20female/chelicera_female_long.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":132,"uid":"a6949fb2-8820-4d29-aac5-8ffd789ef03a","name":"straight","type":0,"feature":60,"images":[{"caption":"Shape of peturon when viewed from the front<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"The median vertical edge of the peturon is not bowed (not geniculate)","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Viewed%20from%20front/form_straight_1.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Viewed%20from%20front/form_straight_1.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":133,"uid":"c0419918-d6d2-4e50-9589-f9b122cfa7d7","name":"mildly geniculate","type":0,"feature":60,"images":[{"caption":"Shape of petiron when viewed from the front<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Inner surfaces of the chelae gently bow laterally. May have horizontal corrugations on the front face.","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Viewed%20from%20front/form_curved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Viewed%20from%20front/form_curved.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":134,"uid":"87c80430-86ca-4b06-9996-826c0df3ab65","name":"strongly geniculate","type":0,"feature":60,"images":[{"caption":"Shape of petiron when viewed from the front<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) R. Whyte","comments":"Geniculate, that is, very bowed on the inner edge of the chelae. Often with horizontal corrugations on the front face.","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Viewed%20from%20front/form_geniculate.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Viewed%20from%20front/form_geniculate.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":135,"uid":"8daf1606-46be-4571-9b00-b9f468f00930","name":"absent","type":0,"feature":61},{"id":136,"uid":"1d13f8bd-9dae-401c-a9c4-43b2888f0644","name":"present","type":0,"feature":61,"images":[{"caption":"Projection on the front face of the paturon<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Such projections can appear in varying positions, depending on the species. Occasionally there is more than one.","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Spike%20on%20anterior/Anterior%20projrctions.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Spike%20on%20anterior/Anterior%20projrctions.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":137,"uid":"4d071407-82ab-48a5-bd04-3757c11f0dde","name":"absent","type":0,"feature":62,"images":[{"caption":"No projections in the area between the distal tooth rows<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Projections can be of verying sizes and shapes  They also may be found in varying postions, depending on the species","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Terminal%20projection/chelae_distal_unadorned.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Terminal%20projection/chelae_distal_unadorned.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":138,"uid":"4b7b6746-1da4-4813-ad08-a482ae58c4bb","name":"present","type":0,"feature":62,"images":[{"caption":"Projections in the area between the distal tooth rows<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Projections can be of varying sizes and shapes  They also may be found in varying positions, depending on the species","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Terminal%20projection/chelae_distal_adornment.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Terminal%20projection/chelae_distal_adornment.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":139,"uid":"69eb92bc-3614-4b52-92d1-67ab07830ba2","name":"absent","type":0,"feature":63},{"id":140,"uid":"bf902d68-e346-4da8-9d57-3da57aa124f4","name":"present","type":0,"feature":63,"images":[{"caption":"Projection on the rear face of the paturon<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Żabka (QMB)","comments":"Projections can be of varying sizes and shapes  They also may be found in varying positions, depending on the species.","path":"Images/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Toothlike%20projection%20on%20posterior%20surface/chelae_posterior_projection2.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Chelicera%20basal%20segment/Toothlike%20projection%20on%20posterior%20surface/chelae_posterior_projection2.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":141,"uid":"beaec076-3011-42c6-b5a4-224b64683387","name":"None","type":0,"feature":64,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of epigynes without atria<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;)  B.J. Richardson (T) (CSIRO), R. Whyte","comments":"Recessed surfaces, sometimes called atria, fossae or windows, are large visible depressions in the raised outer surface of the epigyne. Some genera do not have this feature.","path":"Images/features/Epigyne%20external/Number%20of%20atria/no_atria.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Epigyne%20external/Number%20of%20atria/no_atria.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":142,"uid":"6a8f0a9d-13ce-4e79-a7db-d82f15a4daa2","name":"One","type":0,"feature":64,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of genera with a single, variously shaped atria<br/>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (TL, BR) (CSIRO), R. Whyte (TR), I.R. Macaulay (BL)","comments":"Recessed surfaces, sometimes called atria, fossae or windows, are large visible depressions in the raised outer surface of the epigyne. A single atrium occurs when the epigynum does not have an obvious raised median guide which would divide the depression into two.","path":"Images/features/Epigyne%20external/Number%20of%20atria/one_atriumA.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Epigyne%20external/Number%20of%20atria/one_atriumA.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":143,"uid":"fe04b5cc-1ff2-4aca-a39c-3e128ca270cb","name":"Two","type":0,"feature":64,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of genera with a pair of variously shaped atria<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Recessed surfaces, sometimes called atria, fossae or windows, are large visible depressions in the raised outer surface of the epigyne. Two atria occur when the epigynum has an obvious raised median guide which divides the depression into two.","path":"Images/features/Epigyne%20external/Number%20of%20atria/two_atria.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Epigyne%20external/Number%20of%20atria/two_atria.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":144,"uid":"69068c55-b72e-42e5-9107-2f2239dc7fe8","name":"Without pockets","type":0,"feature":65,"images":[{"caption":"Example of an epigyne without a pocket<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;)  B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Pockets in the epigastric fold may have varying functions; some are the site of the gonopores, others may act as guides during mating.","path":"Images/features/Epigyne%20external/Pockets/pocket_%20absent.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Epigyne%20external/Pockets/pocket_%20absent.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":145,"uid":"cb07a2e5-996e-4408-830f-d3dd4587dc43","name":"With single median pocket","type":0,"feature":65,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of median pockets<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;)  B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Pockets in the epigastric fold may have varying functions; some are the site of the gonopores, others may act as guides during mating. They vary in size from a simple niche in the epigatric fold to a very deep pocket or hood.","path":"Images/features/Epigyne%20external/Pockets/pocket_singleA.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Epigyne%20external/Pockets/pocket_singleA.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":146,"uid":"98ee7df8-ce15-440e-a8bb-e1f14ea609e0","name":"With lateral pockets","type":0,"feature":65,"images":[{"caption":"Examples of lateral pockets<br/>Illustrator (and &copy;)  B.J. Richardson (CSIRO)","comments":"Pockets in the epigastric fold may have varying functions; some are the site of the gonopores, others may act as guides during mating.","path":"Images/features/Epigyne%20external/Pockets/Pockets_pair.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/features/Epigyne%20external/Pockets/Pockets_pair.jpg","type":