mbs.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/salticidae/figure_2_limbs.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Orientation terms.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Zabka (QMB), B.J. Richardson (CSIRO).</p>","comments":"<p>These terms refer to directions not positions.</p>","path":"Images/entities/salticidae/figure_3_directions.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/salticidae/figure_3_directions.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":2,"uid":"f28bd521-2c4d-4f66-b2a2-2c0cbac565ba","name":"Abracadabrella Zabka, 1991","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Abracadabrella elegans.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) R. Whyte.</p>","comments":"<p>Note the fly-like appearance of the genus with 'eyes' at rear end of the abdomen.</p>","path":"Images/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991/plate_abracadabrella_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991/plate_abracadabrella_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Abracadabrella elegans, E. lewiston (RT) and A. birdsville (RB).</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J, Richardson (CSIRO) &amp; M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991/plate_abracadabrella_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991/plate_abracadabrella_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp morphology of Abracadabrella sp.(L) and A. elegans (R).</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991/plate_abracadabrella_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991/plate_abracadabrella_palp.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Epigyne morphology of Abracadabrella elegans.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (TL) (CSIRO), R. Whyte (BL), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/abracadabrella_zabka_1991/plate_abraca