IRO), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/hypoblemum_peckham__peckham_1886/plate_hypoblemum_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/hypoblemum_peckham__peckham_1886/plate_hypoblemum_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":38,"uid":"2b62655a-06e7-4490-88ba-69b029e68c64","name":"Jacksonoides Wanless, 1988","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Jacksonoides.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) I.R. Macaulay (TR, R. Whyte.</p>","comments":"<p>Jacksonoides kochi (TL), J. queenslandicus (BL) &amp; J. distinctus (R).</p>","path":"Images/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Jacksonoides.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO) &amp; M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Note the distinctive pattern of the legs folding upwards when preserved. This is found only very rarely in other genera.</p>","path":"Images/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the chelicera of Jacksonoides.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO) &amp; M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Note the distinctively different patterns of the teeth and paturon projections in males (T) and females (B).</p>","path":"Images/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_preserved5.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_preserved5.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp and epigyne morphology of Jacksonoides kochi.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_genitaliaa.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jacksonoides_wanless_1988/plate_jacksonoides_genitaliaa.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":39,"uid":"b088ade9-f11b-432f-856d-c0a520c0f7b7","name":"Jotus L. Koch, 1881","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Jotus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte (BL) &amp; I.R. Macaulay.</p>","path":"Images/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/plate_jotus_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/plate_jotus_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Jotus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO) M. Zabka (diag,) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/plate_jotus_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/plate_jotus_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp morphology of Jotus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/plate_jotus_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/plate_jotus_palp.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Epigyne morphology of Jotus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), R. whyte (BL).</p>","path":"Images/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/palp_jotus_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/jotus_l._koch_1881/palp_jotus_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":40,"uid":"975c2f9f-d4f0-4b46-aaef-d335ccd27ee2","name":"Judalana Rix, 1999","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/judalana_rix_1999.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Judalana.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) R. Whyte.</p>","path":"Images/entities/judalana_rix_1999/plate_judala_live_.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/judalana_rix_1999/plate_judala_live_.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Judalana.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO). M.G. Rix (diag,) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Note the unusual projection on theface of the paturon (arrowed)..</p>","path":"Images/entities/judalana_rix_1999/plate_judalana_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/judalana_rix_1999/plate_judalana_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp and epigyne morphology of Judalana.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte (TM), B.J. Richardson (B) (CSIRO), M.G. Rix (diag,) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/judalana_rix_1999/plate_judalana_genitalia1.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/judalana_rix_1999/plate_judalana_genitalia1.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":41,"uid":"478d913a-f631-4e3b-9fbc-4ed0360615b9","name":"Ligonipes Karsch, 1878","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Ligonipes.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) R. Whyte.</p>","path":"Images/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Ligonipes.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Żabka (diag,) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_preserved_2.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_preserved_2.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Examples of Ligonipes palps.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte, M. Zabka (diag,) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_palp.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Epigyne morphology of Ligonipes.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (L) (CSIRO), M. Żabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ligonipes_karsch_1878/plate_ligonipes_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":42,"uid":"db570048-f282-463b-a210-0a02387fc492","name":"Maddisonia Zabka, 2014","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/maddisonia_zabka_2014.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Maddisonia.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO).</p>","path":"Images/entities/maddisonia_zabka_2014/plate_maddisonia_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/maddisonia_zabka_2014/plate_maddisonia_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp morphology of Maddisonia.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag.) (AMS)).</p>","comments":"<p>Maddisonia sp., M. whytei (M), M. berbeckai (R). The morphology of the female is unknown.</p>","path":"Images/entities/maddisonia_zabka_2014/plate_maddisonia_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/maddisonia_zabka_2014/plate_maddisonia_palp.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":43,"uid":"1552f8d1-4312-4c2d-b5a7-4043a56b35d6","name":"Maratus Karsch, 1878","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/maratus_karsch_1878.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Maratus.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) J. Otto.</p>","comments":"<p>Note the differences in morphology and colouring between the males and females; pair (BL), female (TL)., males (remainder).</p>","path":"Images/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_maratrus_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_maratrus_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Maratus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J, Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag,) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Note the differences between the male (TM &TL) and females (BM &amp; BL) of Maratus amabilis. The fringed leg 3 (diag,) is used in display. The patterning varies a great deal between species (BR). When folded the flap (if present) curves under the abdomen (TR, arrowed). Some species presently placed in Maratus do not have the brightly coloured abdomens seen in most forms.</p>","path":"Images/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_maratus_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_maratus_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp, chelae and face morphology of Maratus amabilis.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_palp_and_face.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_palp_and_face.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Epigyne morphology of Maratus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Note the species specific differences in the shape of the insemination duct.</p>","path":"Images/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_maratus_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/maratus_karsch_1878/plate_maratus_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":44,"uid":"5bb0be0d-4756-4e84-9d8b-3e0a65b28488","name":"Margaromma Keyserling, 1882","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/margaromma_keyserling_1882.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Margaromma.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), R. Whyte (M), M. Zabka (diag.).</p>","comments":"<p>Margaromma sp (L, BM), and M. funestum (TM, R).</p>","path":"Images/entities/margaromma_keyserling_1882/plate_margaromma_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/margaromma_keyserling_1882/plate_margaromma_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp morphology of Margaromma.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO).</p>","path":"Images/entities/margaromma_keyserling_1882/plate_margaromma_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/margaromma_keyserling_1882/plate_margaromma_palp.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Epigyne morphology of Margaromma.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte (TL), B.J. Richardson (BL), M. Zabka (diag.).</p>","comments":"<p>Margaromma funestum and Margaromma sp.. (BL).</p>","path":"Images/entities/margaromma_keyserling_1882/plate_margaromma_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/margaromma_keyserling_1882/plate_margaromma_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":45,"uid":"51306638-3c7e-435a-9733-aa89b4021336","name":"Megaloastia Zabka, 1995","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Megaloastia.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) F. Soley (TR, BL), R. Mc Ginley (TL), S. Collins, (BR).</p>","comments":"<p>This species lives on the ceiling of rock overhangs and runs rather than jumps.</p>","path":"Images/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plate_megaloastia_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plate_megaloastia_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Megaloastia.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag.) (WAMP).</p>","comments":"<p>Males and females are differently marked: female (TR, BL).</p>","path":"Images/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plare_megaloastia_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plare_megaloastia_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp morphology of Megaloastia.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) M. Zabka (WAMP).</p>","path":"Images/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plate_megaloastia_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plate_megaloastia_palp.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Epigyne morphology of Megaloastia.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag.) (WAMP).</p>","path":"Images/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plate_megaloastia_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/megaloastia_zabka_1995/plate_megaloastia_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id