ohilimia_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ohilimia_strand_1911/plate_ohilimia_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Ohilimia scutellata.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag,) (QMB).</p>","path":"Images/entities/ohilimia_strand_1911/plate_ohilimia_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ohilimia_strand_1911/plate_ohilimia_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp morphology of Ohilimia.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte, M. Zabka (diag.).</p>","path":"Images/entities/ohilimia_strand_1911/plate_ohilimia_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ohilimia_strand_1911/plate_ohilimia_palp.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Epigyne morphology of Ohilimia.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte, M. Zabka (dig.).</p>","path":"Images/entities/ohilimia_strand_1911/plate_ohilimia_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/ohilimia_strand_1911/plate_ohilimia_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":54,"uid":"ffe026a6-7e76-42ec-8855-6bce14679a5f","name":"Opisthoncus L. Koch, 1880","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Examples of live Opisthoncus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte (T), I.R. Macaulay.</p>","comments":"<p>Opisthoncus sp. (TR), O. polyphemus (TR), O. serratofasciatus (ML), O. tenuipes (MR, BL, BR)),.</p>","path":"Images/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_live_.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_live_.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Opisthoncus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte, B.J. Richardson (TM, ML) (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag.) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Not the range of morphologies found in the male chelae. Arrow shows the position of the median prominence found in most Opisthoncus species. The patterns of teeth and paturon projections diverges between males and females of the same species (diagrams BR).</p>","path":"Images/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_preserved.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_preserved.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Palp morphology of Opisthoncus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte, M. Zabka (diag,) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Note the range of morphologies found between species. It is very likely that Opisthoncus is polyphyletic. Opisthoncus keyserlingi (TL), O polyphemus (BL), O. grassator (M), O. mordax (R) and O. paracedentatus (diag,).</p>","path":"Images/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_palp.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_palp.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Examples of the epigyne morphology of Opisthoncus.</p><br/><p>Illustrators (and &copy;) R. Whyte (TL), B.J. Richardson (BL) (CSIRO), M. Zabka (diag,) (QMB).</p>","comments":"<p>Opisthoncus polyphemis, O. sp. and O. parcidentatus (diag.).</p>","path":"Images/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_epigyne.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/opisthoncus_l._koch_1880/plate_opisthoncus_epigyne.jpg","type":1}]},{"id":55,"uid":"d6d2744c-e80a-465d-a73e-a4e08c4def09","name":"Papuaneon Maddison 2016","type":1,"children":false,"parent":1,"text":[{"caption":"Fact Sheet","path":"Html/entities/papuaneon_maddison_2016.htm","type":2}],"images":[{"caption":"<p>Example of live Papuaneon.</p><br/><p>Illustraor (and &copy;) R. Whyte.</p>","path":"Images/entities/papuaneon_maddison_2016/plate_papuaneon_live.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/papuaneon_maddison_2016/plate_papuaneon_live.jpg","type":1},{"caption":"<p>Aspects of the general morphology of Papuaneon.</p><br/><p>Illustrator (and &copy;) B.J. Richardson (CSIRO, MP).</p>","path":"Images/entities/papuaneon_maddison_2016/papuaneon_mrphology.jpg","thumb_path":"Thumbs/entities/papuaneon_maddison_2016/papuaneon_mrphology.jpg","type":1},{"